# Post-primitives docket reminder

Track follow-ups in `packages/ui/.migration/post-primitives-docket.md`.

## When to remind the user

**Proactively remind** (short nudge + link the docket) when any of these happen:

1. The last thin-pass stub under `packages/ui/src/primitives/` is being
   Figma-matched or consciously closed out.
2. `packages/ui/src/primitives/README.md` no longer lists thin-pass stubs (or
   the user says primitives / shadcn pass is “done”).
3. The user asks what to do next after primitives, or starts a broad “polish /
   composition” pass across the design system.

## While primitives are still in progress

- Do **not** nag every session.
- When skipping a composition because a partner primitive is missing or
  thin-pass, **add a docket checkbox** (and a **Deferred** note on that
  primitive’s README) instead of silently dropping it.

## Do not

- Block finishing a primitive on docket items.
- Invent new backlog files — extend the docket above.
